    "text": "To solve the expression \\((x + 1 - x)! \\div (x - x + 1)!\\), let's first simplify the terms inside the factorial expressions.\n\n### Step 1: Simplify the terms inside the factorials\n- The first term is \\(x + 1 - x\\). This simplifies to:\n  \\[\n  x + 1 - x = 1\n  \\]\n- The second term is \\(x - x + 1\\). This simplifies to:\n  \\[\n  x - x + 1 = 1\n  \\]\n\n### Step 2: Substitute the simplified terms back into the expression\nNow, substitute these simplified terms back into the original expression:\n\\[\n(1)! \\div (1)!\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Evaluate the factorials\nThe factorial of 1 is:\n\\[\n1! = 1\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Perform the division\nThe expression now becomes:\n\\[\n1 \\div 1 = 1\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\nThus, the value of \\((x + 1 - x)! \\div (x - x + 1)!\\) in simplest form is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]",
